  "scenes": {
    "sm-detail": {
      "anchor": "sm-a",
      "offset": [1.5, 3.5, 1.6],
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "smem",
          "name": "L1 / Shared memory",
          "group": "memory",
          "color": "#e0a33a",
          "geom": {
            "type": "box",
            "size": [3.4, 0.2, 2.4],
            "pos": [0, 0, 0]
          },
          "desc": "Programmable scratchpad shared by the threads of a block. TMA fills it with A/B tiles; Tensor Cores read operands straight from here.",
          "specs": [
            {
              "label": "L1 + shared (per SM)",
              "value": "256 KB (up to 228 KB shared)",
              "source": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/nvidia-hopper-architecture-in-depth/"
            }
          ],
          "role": "shared-memory"
        },
        {
          "id": "cluster-link",
          "parent": "smem",
          "name": "Thread Block Cluster (DSMEM)",
          "group": "io",
          "color": "#2f9e6e",
          "geom": {
            "type": "box",
            "size": [1.3, 0.15, 0.55],
            "pos": [1.15, -0.2, -1.4]
          },
          "desc": "Thread Block Clusters co-schedule several blocks across SMs in the same GPC. The SM-to-SM network lets one block load, store, and atomically update another block's shared memory directly — distributed shared memory (DSMEM) — without a trip through L2.",
          "specs": [
            {
              "label": "Max cluster size",
              "value": "8 blocks portable (up to 16 non-portable)",
              "source": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/nvidia-hopper-architecture-in-depth/"
            }
          ],
          "role": "distributed-shared-memory"
        },
        {
          "id": "tensor-core",
          "parent": "smem",
          "name": "Tensor Core (4th gen)",
          "group": "compute",
          "color": "#2a58b8",
          "geom": {
            "type": "box",
            "size": [0.7, 0.35, 0.9],
            "pos": [-1.25, 0.5, -0.55]
          },
          "repeat": {
            "count": [4, 1, 1],
            "step": [0.83, 0, 0]
          },
          "desc": "Multiplies matrix tiles per warpgroup instruction (wgmma). The Transformer Engine drives FP8 precision here, recasting and rescaling tensors layer by layer. Accumulators live in registers — Hopper has no TMEM.",
          "specs": [
            {
              "label": "Low-precision format",
              "value": "FP8 (E4M3, E5M2) via Transformer Engine",
              "source": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/nvidia-hopper-architecture-in-depth/"
            }
          ],
          "role": "tensor-core"
        },
        {
          "id": "register-file",
          "parent": "smem",
          "name": "Register file",
          "group": "memory",
          "color": "#d07a40",
          "geom": {
            "type": "box",
            "size": [0.7, 0.25, 0.9],
            "pos": [-1.25, 0.45, 0.55]
          },
          "repeat": {
            "count": [4, 1, 1],
            "step": [0.83, 0, 0]
          },
          "desc": "Per-thread registers. On Hopper they also hold Tensor Core accumulators.",
          "specs": [
            {
              "label": "Size (per SM)",
              "value": "256 KB (4 × 64 KB)",
              "estimate": true
            }
          ],
          "role": "register-file"
        },
        {
          "id": "warp-scheduler",
          "parent": "register-file",
          "name": "Warp scheduler + CUDA cores",
          "group": "control",
          "geom": {
            "type": "box",
            "size": [0.7, 0.15, 0.9],
            "pos": [-1.25, 0.75, 0.55]
          },
          "repeat": {
            "count": [4, 1, 1],
            "step": [0.83, 0, 0]
          },
          "desc": "Each cycle picks a ready warp (32 threads) to issue. Scalar CUDA cores (FP32/INT32) run the epilogue: bias, activation, quantization.",
          "role": "warp-scheduler"
        },
        {
          "id": "tma",
          "parent": "smem",
          "name": "TMA (Tensor Memory Accelerator)",
          "group": "io",
          "geom": {
            "type": "box",
            "size": [1.6, 0.15, 0.4],
            "pos": [-0.9, -0.25, 1.4]
          },
          "desc": "Copies whole multi-dimensional tensor tiles between L2/HBM and shared memory asynchronously, without spending threads. Can also push a tile straight into another SM's shared memory within a Thread Block Cluster.",
          "role": "tma"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "flows": [
    {
      "id": "hbm-left",
      "from": "hbm-dram-left",
      "to": "die",
      "group": "memory",
      "particles": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "hbm-right",
      "from": "hbm-dram-right",
      "to": "die",
      "group": "memory",
      "particles": 2
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "1. Weights sit in HBM3 (80 GB, 5 of 6 stacks active, 3.35 TB/s).",
      "focus": ["hbm-dram-left", "hbm-dram-right", "hbm-base-left", "hbm-base-right", "hbm-site-empty"],
      "dot": "hbm-dram-left",
      "explode": 0.6,
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "hbm"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. Memory controllers read the HBM stacks.",
      "focus": ["mc-left"],
      "dot": "mc-left",
      "stage": "memory-controller"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. Data lands in the 50 MB L2 cache.",
      "focus": ["l2"],
      "dot": "l2",
      "stage": "l2"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. TMA copies A and B tiles into shared memory, asynchronously.",
      "focus": ["tma"],
      "dot": "tma",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "tma"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. Tiles sit in shared memory, ready for the Tensor Cores.",
      "focus": ["smem"],
      "dot": "smem",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "shared-memory"
    },
    {
      "text": "6. A Thread Block Cluster can fetch a tile straight from a neighboring SM's shared memory (DSMEM), skipping L2.",
      "focus": ["cluster-link"],
      "dot": "cluster-link",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "thread-block-cluster"
    },
    {
      "text": "7. A warpgroup issues wgmma: Tensor Cores multiply the tiles, e.g. in FP8 via the Transformer Engine.",
      "focus": ["tensor-core"],
      "dot": "tensor-core",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "tensor-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "8. Partial sums accumulate in registers — Hopper has no Tensor Memory.",
      "focus": ["register-file"],
      "dot": "register-file",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "accumulate"
    },
    {
      "text": "9. Epilogue: CUDA cores add bias, apply activation, quantize.",
      "focus": ["warp-scheduler", "register-file"],
      "dot": "warp-scheduler",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "epilogue"
    },
    {
      "text": "10. Results go back to HBM; with tensor parallelism, NVLink all-reduces with other GPUs.",
      "focus": ["nvlink"],
      "dot": "nvlink",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "writeback"
    }
  ],
